<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Guerrero state partial election results.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Guerrero state partial election results.</headline>
<dateline>CHILPANCINGO, Mexico 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Partial results from Mexico's Guerrero state town hall elections held Sunday were released Monday by the Guerrero State Electoral Council.</p>
<p>    City	    Pct Vote Counted    Party	  Votes Counted</p>
<p>    Acapulco		76 pct	   PAN		13,266</p>
<p>						   PRI		41,592</p>
<p>						   PRD		36,308</p>
<p>    Coyuca		  59 pct	   PAN		   568</p>
<p>						   PRI		 4,895</p>
<p>						   PRD		 3,700</p>
<p>    Chilpancingo	  68 pct	   PAN		 1,224</p>
<p>						   PRI		12,579</p>
<p>						   PRD		 5,128</p>
<p>    Iguala		  83 pct	   PAN		   827</p>
<p>						   PRI		 9,435</p>
<p>						   PRD		12,503</p>
<p>    Taxco		   76 pct	   PAN		 7,700</p>
<p>						   PRI		 7,227</p>
<p>						   PRD		 1,999</p>
<p>    Atoyac		  51 pct	   PAN		   102</p>
<p>						   PRI		 4,158</p>
<p>						   PRD		 3,713</p>
<p>The PAN is the pro-business the National Action Party, the PRI is the ruling Institutional Revolutionary Party, the PRD is the leftist Democratic Revolution Party.</p>
<p>-- David Luhnow, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289560</p>
